                           AsterIDE Project Notes
                            Version 1.0, July 2026

                      GENERAL INFORMATION AND GUIDELINES

    1. Purpose.

    This file exists as a lightweight repository notebook. It may contain
    project notes, architectural ideas, implementation reminders, or
    temporary information that does not belong in the documentation.

    2. Goals.

    The long-term goals of AsterIDE are:

    (a) simplicity over feature count

    (b) predictable behavior

    (c) low resource usage

    (d) portability across supported platforms (even android)

    (e) maintainable and readable source code

    3. Architecture.

    When adding new functionality, contributors should prefer extending
    existing systems before introducing entirely new ones.

    Complex solutions should only be used when simpler alternatives have
    been evaluated and found insufficient.

    4. Notes.

    This section may be freely updated during development with temporary
    ideas, implementation plans, or reminders.

    Example entries:

    - investigate incremental rendering
    - improve file tree performance
    - profile startup time
    - review editor command architecture

    5. Miscellaneous.

    Content contained within this file is informational only and does not
    constitute project policy. Official project rules are documented in
    CONTRIBUTING, SECURITY, LICENSE, CODE_OF_CONDUCT and other repository
    documentation.

    END OF PROJECT NOTES
